I think to_string shouldn't be used because it may return unexpected results: see here http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string/to_string (for 1e-9 it returns "0.000000")

You have two alternatives:
1. Use QString and its arg method. This works similarly to printf & friends
2. Use std::stringstream
`
#include <sstream>
std::stringstream stream;
stream << std::setprecision(12) << std::fixed << value;
std::string str = stream.str();
`

