Testing this is a bit more tricky because when compiling the hard-coded string its content is different.

So, to test it you have to set the path in the debugging parameters of the FreeCADMain target. And inside ExtractUserPath() this code snippet is needed:
```C++
    QString path = QString::fromUtf8(_argv[1]);
    std::wstring wstr = path.toStdWString();
    const WCHAR* szPath = wstr.c_str();
```

So, when encoding the string to UTF-8 and passing it to boost::filesystem::path the test will fail. Fortunately, boost::filesystem::path also accepts wide string and szPath can be directly passed. So, we don't even need the function calls of WideCharToMultiByte any more.

