The structure of MatrixPy::move() and MatrixPy::scale() is actually wrong. I don't know who originally wrote it that way but doing
```
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
...
}
else if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
   PyErr_Clear();
...
}
else if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
   PyErr_Clear();
...
}
```

doesn't work reliably. Once you called PyArg_ParseTuple() and it returns false you cannot immediately call it again with different arguments. It will work in most cases but in some rare cases it will fail when it should succeed.

The two functions (I haven't checked if there are more) should be restructured to:
```
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
   return ...;
}

PyErr_Clear();
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
   return ...;
}

PyErr_Clear();
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(args, ...)) {
   return ...;
}
```

