@Kuzma30 So I think you don't get it. ;)
Using `QObject::tr()` will generate translation strings without context (they will be pushed in an "unclassified" category) so it makes it hard for translator to now where they come from. Also it creates risk of collisions.
Setting `Q_DECLARE_TR_FUNCTIONS(class_name)` macro in the class declaration will add to it "contextualized" translate functions. So then you only use `tr()` function in the class implementation, and the translation strings will be extracted with an helpful usage context. ;)

