A more serious fix (not caused by this PR): 2041eca74c

If the call of `PyArg_ParseTuple` returns false you can immediately call it again. Instead you must call PyErr_Clear() beforehand. Thus, a code structure of this form is not possible:
```
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(...)) {
...
}
else if (PyArg_ParseTuple(...)) {
}
```

You have to write
```
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(...)) {
...
    return;
}

PyErr_Clear();
if (PyArg_ParseTuple(...)) {
...
    return;
}
```

