Clang-format, with the current settings, reorders the headers (within a block of headers). Many Python binding files XXXPyImp.cpp, have the two includes (cpp and h) in a row:

```
#include "SketchObjectSFPy.h"
#include "SketchObjectSFPy.cpp"
```
Reordering them causes the compilation process to fail.

The solution I found is to leave a blank line to avoid the reorder:
```
#include "SketchObjectSFPy.h"

#include "SketchObjectSFPy.cpp"
```

I am sure this will be widely known. It was not for me, so I comment it here. Perhaps it is useful for somebody, or somebody knows a better/preferred alternative way.

